### Evaluating the Agile Process

#### Pros of Scrum‑Agile in the SNHU Travel Project

- Adaptability to changing requirements  
- Continuous stakeholder feedback  
- Early delivery of working software  
- Improved communication  
- Reduced risk of late‑stage failures  

#### Cons

- Requires consistent stakeholder involvement  
- Frequent meetings may feel time‑consuming  
- Scope creep can occur if backlog management is weak  
- Team members must be disciplined and self‑organized  

#### Was Scrum‑Agile the Best Approach?

Scrum‑Agile was the best approach for the SNHU Travel project. The project involved evolving requirements, user‑focused features, and iterative design — all of which align well with Agile principles. A waterfall approach would have struggled with mid‑project changes and delayed feedback. Scrum allowed the team to deliver value continuously, adapt quickly, and maintain strong communication throughout development.

